<title>USA: United International CFO resigns.</title>
<headline>United International CFO resigns.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER, Colo. 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>United International Holdings Inc said on Monday that J. Timothy Bryan would replace Bernie Dvorak as chief financial officer, effective December 2.</p>
<p>Dvorak resigned to pursue other interests, the television services company said.</p>
<p>Bryan was previously vice president of finance and treasurer of Jones Financial Group, an affiliate of Jones International Ltd.</p>
<p>Dvorak agreed to remain with the company through the end of the year to assist with the transition, the company said.</p>
